# Scoops an escape pod, and meets a boulder the scoops cannot take. It starts from scooping-an-escape-pod.cdr
# (Tools/PrepareCommanders.py): the commander mining-laser.replay starts from, with fuel scoops and a mining laser, but
# with the random state 154,569 draws on, which spawns an escape pod 7,200 units ahead 2.2 s into flight.
# Steered to pass under the nose, as scooping-a-canister.replay's barrel is, it is scooped (TryScoopObject): Escape Pod
# Retrieved...Slaves!, a tonne of slaves into the hold. A boulder spawns next; steered under the nose too, it shows
# SCOOP RETRIEVAL INACTIVE, then rams the ship and is destroyed, for a bounty of 0.1 credits. The draw count was found
# by a search of 1,000 counts for the soonest escape pod scooped, and again, 31 counts on, when the clock became
# milliseconds (D87); the flight was played by a scratch program that steered each object to pass 100 units under the
# nose every 50 ms, then the boulder straight in, and what it pressed is recorded here.
file JAMESON.CDR scooping-an-escape-pod.cdr
wait 0.5; key space; wait 3.5      # any key: the credits, then the status screen
key Escape; wait 0.3               # D10, Disc access, on Load commander
key 1; wait 0.3                    # Load commander: the catalogue, JAMESON.CDR selected
key Return; wait 0.5               # loaded
